  "body": "## What changed\n- Added `operation::extend_to_loop_in(world, setup, picks)` in `crates/app/src/operation/boundary_picks.rs` and re-exported it in `crates/app/src/operation/mod.rs`.\n- Replaced `model::transform_of` with `setup_align::pose_in(world, &e, setup)` inside `extend_to_loop_in`. Face normals now rotate into the setup's part-alignment frame, matching `OpFrame::pose_in_setup` in `selection.rs`.\n- Updated `operation::extend_to_loop(world, picks)` to call `extend_to_loop_in` with `setup::active(world)`, matching the viewport's `view_pose`.\n- Updated `boundary_draft::extend` in `crates/ui/src/boundary_draft.rs` and `edge_pick::take_loop` in `crates/ui/src/edge_pick.rs` to pass the operation's `setup` to `extend_to_loop_in`.\n- Added decision note `docs/decisions/2216-extend-to-loop-setup-align.md`.\n\n## Cause\n`boundary_picks::extend_to_loop` read `model::transform_of(world, &e)` and ignored the setup's `part_alignment`. Pure Z turns and 180-degree X/Y flips keep `|n.z|` unchanged (`|-n.z| == |n.z|`), so they matched by coincidence. A 90-degree flip onto a side or a free angle tilts Z, so `extend_to_loop` picked the model-frame horizontal face instead of the setup-frame horizontal face.\n\n## Tests\n- `area_picks::extend_to_loop_reads_face_normals_in_the_setup_frame`: RED before fix on `[90.0, 0.0, 0.0]`; GREEN after fix for `180° X`, `90° Z`, `90° X`, `55° X`, active `Setup2`, and `extend_to_loop_in` with `Setup1` active.\n- `boundary_picks::extend_to_loop_button_uses_the_operations_aligned_setup`: pins `boundary_draft::extend` on `Setup2` (`90° X`) while `Setup1` is active.\n- `edge_loop_pick::shift_click_on_an_aligned_setup_closes_around_the_setup_horizontal_face`: pins `edge_pick::queue_edge_pick` with Shift on `Setup2` (`90° X`) while `Setup1` is active.\n- Mutation 1 (revert `setup_align::pose_in` to `model::transform_of` in `extend_to_loop_in`): `area_picks::extend_to_loop_reads_face_normals_in_the_setup_frame` FAILS -> restored -> PASSES.\n- Mutation 2 (revert `boundary_draft::extend` to `extend_to_loop`): `boundary_picks::extend_to_loop_button_uses_the_operations_aligned_setup` FAILS -> restored -> PASSES.\n- Mutation 3 (revert `edge_pick::take_loop` to `extend_to_loop`): `edge_loop_pick::shift_click_on_an_aligned_setup_closes_around_the_setup_horizontal_face` FAILS -> restored -> PASSES.\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` PASSED (`wall 15.6 min, 2 step(s), 0 failed`: all 224 `camcraft-app` suites and all `camcraft-ui` suites).\n- Clippy: `env -u RUSTC_WRAPPER cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` PASSED (0 warnings).\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone (`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` returned empty).\n\n## Review visual evidence\nActual shell and GPU viewport captures from the same fixture, with Setup2 active and its part alignment rotated 90° about X. Before captures temporarily restore the old `model::transform_of` lookup; after captures use this PR head. The old lookup selects the vertical model-top face. The fix selects the horizontal face in the aligned setup. Both captures use the same camera and picked edge.\n\n| Action | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Extend to loop | ![Extend before: vertical face loop](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/1874a187aa3c58f81624f82571aa43aa317023e1/2281/extend-before.png) | ![Extend after: aligned horizontal face loop](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/1874a187aa3c58f81624f82571aa43aa317023e1/2281/extend-after.png) |\n| Shift-click edge loop | ![Shift-click before: vertical face loop](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/1874a187aa3c58f81624f82571aa43aa317023e1/2281/shift-click-before.png) | ![Shift-click after: aligned horizontal face loop](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/1874a187aa3c58f81624f82571aa43aa317023e1/2281/shift-click-after.png) |\n\nImages are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch. No images or capture harness were committed to the PR branch. The existing Extend and Shift-click pins both failed under the temporary lookup mutation and passed after restoration.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No interactive mouse-driven GUI session ran. The captures above render the real shell and GPU viewport through the temporary test harness; existing state tests exercise `boundary_draft::extend` and `edge_pick::queue_edge_pick`.\n- `boundary_draft::take_pick` still calls `extend_to_loop` (using `setup::active`, matching `view_pose`) rather than `extend_to_loop_in`, so it does not touch the function edited by open PR #2149.\n\n## Overlaps\n- `crates/ui/src/boundary_draft.rs`: PR #2149 edits `take_pick` and `refresh_preview` (different functions from `extend`; whichever merges second refreshes).\n- `crates/app/src/operation/mod.rs`: PRs #2162, #2136, and #2035 touch different lines of this file (whichever merges second refreshes). PR #1738 lists `boundary_picks.rs` and `operation/mod.rs` against an older unmerged base, with no edits to `boundary_picks.rs` relative to `upstream/main`.\n\nEffort: medium\nChangelog: Boundary \"Extend to loop\" and Shift-click loop selection now read face normals in the setup's part-alignment frame.\nFixes #2216\n",
